# The pentagrid, the regular tiling {5, 4}, right-angled pentagons four to a vertex, the canonical hyperbolic grid and
# the origin of Margenstern's whole program (the "five is missing" joke: a regular pentagon tiles no flat plane, but in
# the hyperbolic plane, where angles can be smaller, a right-angled pentagon tiles perfectly). It is the stage for the
# splitting method, Fibonacci addressing, fast SAT, and a weakly universal cellular automaton. Two arithmetic facts are
# machine-checked by `seed test`: that it is hyperbolic, and the Fibonacci growth of its tile tree.

# The pentagrid is hyperbolic by the Schläfli test: (p - 2)(q - 2) is above 4. Here (5 - 2)(4 - 2) = 3 * 2 = 6, above 4.
# A spherical or flat grid would fail this.
hold pentagrid-is-hyperbolic
  call is-above
    call multiply
      call subtract
        code 5
        code 2
      call subtract
        code 4
        code 2
    code 4

# The tile tree grows by the Fibonacci recurrence: each generation count is the sum of the two before it. The pentagrid
# counts run 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13. Three is two plus one, five is three plus two, eight is five plus three, thirteen is
# eight plus five. A wrong count breaks the recurrence.
hold third-pentagrid-generation-is-first-two-summed
  call is-equal
    call add
      code 1
      code 2
    code 3
hold fourth-pentagrid-generation-is-prior-two-summed
  call is-equal
    call add
      code 2
      code 3
    code 5
hold fifth-pentagrid-generation-is-prior-two-summed
  call is-equal
    call add
      code 3
      code 5
    code 8
hold sixth-pentagrid-generation-is-prior-two-summed
  call is-equal
    call add
      code 5
      code 8
    code 13
